* YHDC SCT-013-000 split-core current transformer, 100 A : 50 mA
*
* Pins: P1 P2 TIP SLEEVE
*   P1 -> P2  primary conductor through the core (zero-impedance current sense)
*   TIP/SLEEVE secondary (3.5 mm plug). TIP goes positive for current P1 -> P2.
*
* Linear equivalent circuit referred to the secondary:
*
*   Ip/N --+--- LL --- RW --- TIP
*          |  |
*         LM  CW
*          |  |
*   -------+--+--------------- SLEEVE
*
* N  = 2000 turns (datasheet ratio 100 A : 50 mA)
* LM = magnetising inductance. 5.5 H with RW = 100 ohm reproduces the
*      OpenEnergyMonitor measurements: ~4 deg phase lead with a 22 ohm
*      burden and ~7-8 deg with 120 ohm.
* RW, LL, CW are NOT published. The defaults are estimates. Measure RW with
*      an ohmmeter and fit LL/CW from a frequency sweep before trusting
*      results above a few kHz.
*
* Not modelled: core saturation (starts ~140 A), the ±3 % ratio error,
* the internal TVS that clamps an open secondary.

.subckt SCT013_000 P1 P2 TIP SLEEVE N=2000 LM=5.5 RW=100 LL=0.5m CW=50p
Vsense P1 P2 0
F1 SLEEVE e Vsense {1/N}
Lm e SLEEVE {LM}
Cw e SLEEVE {CW}
Ll e e2 {LL}
Rw e2 TIP {RW}
.ends SCT013_000
